solution:
Use the entries in their given order: \(a=1\), \(b=-2\), and \(c=-3\). The denominator is \(-3-(-2)=-1\), which is nonzero, so
\[
\boxed{1,-2,-3}
=\frac{-3+1}{-3-(-2)}
=\frac{-2}{-1}
=2.
\]
The answer is \(2\), choice \(\mathrm{E}\).

